  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA-only multiprofile models with avgpool aggregation outperform single-profile and transformer-aggregated variants, and scvi_n200 is currently the best RNA encoder. However, scgpt is untested, so there is uncertainty about whether the scvi advantage is encoder-specific or whether another learned RNA representation can match it. config_008 tests scgpt while keeping the currently best profile setting and aggregation fixed, giving a clean comparison against config_005 and config_002. This is a better use of the next budget than moving to multimodal fusion, since image-only performance is weak and the RNA representation choice remains an important unresolved factor."
